    "problem_statement": "Markup.split() method returns incorrect results when using maxsplit parameter\n\nI've found an issue with the `Markup.split()` method in MarkupSafe. When using the `maxsplit` parameter, it doesn't behave the same way as the standard Python string `split()` method.\n\nHere's a simple reproduction case:\n\n```python\nfrom markupsafe import Markup\n\n# This works as expected\nprint(Markup('a b c').split())  # [Markup('a'), Markup('b'), Markup('c')]\n\n# This doesn't work correctly\nprint(Markup('a b c').split(maxsplit=1))  # Should be [Markup('a'), Markup('b c')]\n```\n\nThe issue seems to be that when specifying a maxsplit value, the Markup class doesn't correctly handle the parameter, resulting in unexpected splitting behavior.\n\nFor example, if I try to split a string with a maxsplit of 1, I expect to get two items: the first split item and then the rest of the string as the second item. But the current implementation doesn't respect this behavior.\n\nI'm using MarkupSafe version 2.1.3 with Python 3.10."
